# Always commit and push

After each code change in this repo (Part finder), commit and push to the current branch's upstream without waiting to be asked again.

- Stage only files that belong to the change. Leave secrets out (`.env`, credentials, keys). If one would be committed, warn and do not add it.
- Message: 1–2 sentences, why the change exists, matching recent `git log` style.
- Push with `git push`. Add `-u` only when the branch has no upstream.
- Never force-push. Never skip hooks. Never update git config. Never run destructive git commands unless the user explicitly asks.
- If there is nothing new to commit but the branch is ahead of the remote, still push.
- If there is no remote or push fails, report the exact error and stop.

```powershell
git add -- path/to/changed-files
git commit -m @"
Short sentence on why this change exists.
"@
git push
```
